651 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 383 0 R
/E (The Bible begins with an astonishing truth. Human beings are different from everything else God created. Mountains display His power. The stars display His greatness. The oceans display His majesty. But humanity alone was created in His image.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
652 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 383 0 R
/E (Being created in God's image means that we were made to know Him, love Him, reflect His character, and enjoy fellowship with Him. Our value does not come from what we own or accomplish. Our value comes from the One who created us. Every human life has dignity because every person bears the image of God.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
