<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 384 0 R
/T (2. The Tragedy of Losing Our Identity)
/E (2. The Tragedy of Losing Our Identity)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
667 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 384 0 R
/E (Although humanity was created for fellowship with God, sin entered the world. Sin did more than separate us from God. It distorted how we see ourselves. Instead of living as God's children, people began searching for identity in temporary things. Some pursue acceptance. Others pursue power. Others pursue pleasure. Still others pursue recognition. Yet even after achieving these things, many still feel empty. Why? Because the human heart was created for God. Nothing less can satisfy it.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
